WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.500
Easy Fables. Part 1.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.475
The Fox and the Grapes.

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:07.445
A hungry fox was walking through a garden.

00:00:07.445 --> 00:00:10.429
He saw some sweet grapes high up on a wall.

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:13.283
"Those grapes look so good," he said.

00:00:13.283 --> 00:00:14.666
"I must have them."

00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:18.851
He jumped as high as he could, but he could not reach them.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.825
He tried again and again.

00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:23.257
Each time he fell back to the ground.

00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:26.039
At last he was too tired to jump.

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:28.533
He walked away with his nose in the air.

00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:31.758
"I did not want those grapes anyway," he said.

00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:34.160
"I am sure they are not sweet at all."

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.078
It is easy to say bad things about what you cannot have.

00:00:38.078 --> 00:00:40.021
The Hare and the Tortoise.

00:00:40.021 --> 00:00:43.559
A hare laughed at a tortoise because he was so slow.

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:46.473
"Let us have a race," said the tortoise.

00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:48.073
"I think I can win."

00:00:48.073 --> 00:00:51.351
The hare laughed even more, but he said yes.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:52.708
The race began.

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:56.267
The hare ran very fast and was soon far in front.

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:58.860
"I have lots of time," he thought.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.942
"I will rest under this tree."

00:01:00.942 --> 00:01:03.137
Soon he was fast asleep.

00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:05.325
The tortoise did not stop.

00:01:05.325 --> 00:01:08.992
He walked on, slowly, step after step.

00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:12.025
He passed the sleeping hare and kept going.

00:01:12.025 --> 00:01:15.998
When the hare woke up, he ran as fast as he could.

00:01:15.998 --> 00:01:17.703
But it was too late.

00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:19.890
The tortoise had already won.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.381
Slow and steady wins the race.

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.277
The Lion and the Mouse.

00:01:24.277 --> 00:01:26.837
A lion was sleeping in the forest.

00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:30.182
A little mouse ran over his nose and woke him up.

00:01:30.182 --> 00:01:31.813
The lion was angry.

00:01:31.813 --> 00:01:34.409
He caught the mouse under his big foot.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:37.195
"Please let me go," cried the mouse.

00:01:37.195 --> 00:01:39.219
"One day I will help you."

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:40.708
The lion laughed.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:43.118
How could a little mouse help a lion?

00:01:43.118 --> 00:01:44.678
But he let her go.

00:01:44.678 --> 00:01:49.337
A few days later, some men caught the lion in a strong net.

00:01:49.337 --> 00:01:52.493
He pulled and pulled, but he could not get out.

00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:54.188
He cried out loudly.

00:01:54.188 --> 00:01:56.531
The mouse heard him and came running.

00:01:56.531 --> 00:01:59.223
She bit through the net with her sharp teeth.

00:01:59.223 --> 00:02:01.217
Soon the lion was free.

00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:07.943
"You laughed at me," said the mouse, "but now you see that even a small friend can be a great friend."

00:02:07.943 --> 00:02:10.072
The Boy Who Cried Wolf.

00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:14.023
A boy looked after the sheep on a hill near his village.

00:02:14.023 --> 00:02:17.795
It was quiet up there, and he had nothing to do.

00:02:17.795 --> 00:02:19.849
One day he thought of a game.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:23.149
He ran toward the village and shouted, "Wolf!

00:02:23.149 --> 00:02:24.013
Wolf!

00:02:24.013 --> 00:02:26.026
A wolf is eating the sheep!"

00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:29.529
The people of the village ran up the hill to help him.

00:02:29.529 --> 00:02:31.345
But there was no wolf.

00:02:31.345 --> 00:02:34.558
The boy laughed at them, and they went home angry.

00:02:34.558 --> 00:02:37.673
A few days later he did the same thing again.

00:02:37.673 --> 00:02:41.048
Again the people came, and again he laughed.

00:02:41.048 --> 00:02:43.707
Then one evening a wolf really came.

00:02:43.707 --> 00:02:44.586
"Wolf!

00:02:44.586 --> 00:02:47.000
Wolf!" the boy shouted.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.238
"Please help me!"

00:02:48.238 --> 00:02:50.364
But this time nobody came.

00:02:50.364 --> 00:02:52.689
And the wolf ate many of the sheep.

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:58.861
Nobody believes a person who does not tell the truth, even when he tells the truth at last.

00:02:58.861 --> 00:03:00.834
The Crow and the Water Jar.

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.021
A crow was very thirsty.

00:03:03.021 --> 00:03:07.766
It had not rained for many weeks, and she could not find any water.

00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:10.960
At last she saw a tall jar in a garden.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.626
She flew down to it.

00:03:13.241 --> 00:03:16.061
There was a little water at the bottom of the jar.

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:19.074
But the jar was tall and her mouth was short.

00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:21.129
She could not reach the water.

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:25.176
She tried to push the jar over, but it was too heavy.

00:03:25.176 --> 00:03:26.969
Then she had an idea.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:30.845
She picked up a small stone and dropped it into the jar.

00:03:30.845 --> 00:03:33.762
Then she dropped in another, and another.

00:03:33.762 --> 00:03:37.211
With each stone, the water came up a little higher.

00:03:37.211 --> 00:03:42.555
At last the water was near the top, and the crow drank as much as she wanted.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.553
If you think hard, you can often find a way.
